      "writtenOn": "2025-01-23T01:01:32Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "SHA-256 support (CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA256) was already enabled, due to being selected by IPsec support (CONFIG_XFRM_ESP).  SHA-256 *acceleration* using ARMv8 CE (CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA2_ARM64_CE) was not enabled, so SHA-256 performance was about 10x slower than necessary.  Please check the previous CL, which I just added you to Cc on.\n \nBy the way, I doubt that microdroid needs IPsec support.  Probably it doesn\u0027t even need networking support?  Disabling all (or at least most of) the networking support would provide a large savings too.\n\nI could have used menuconfig, but I just edited it manually and then used savedefconfig and verified that nothing else needed to be changed.  Please note that the file already was not clean when doing through a savedefconfig cycle, though.  It would be a good idea to enforce that, like is already done for gki_defconfig.",
      "parentUuid": "105ba9c2_0df87247",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "f081fb3b30b0d28637e7462be70f2a28b3d9032a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
